\lispPackageChapter{chorus/interop}

This package is a separate system, \texttt{chorus-interop}. It depends on
\texttt{chorus}, \texttt{cl-opengl}, \texttt{cl-glu}, and \texttt{cl-glut}.
Load it with \texttt{(ql:quickload :chorus-interop)}.

It reexports \texttt{chorus/lang}, the interop API, and the driver variables
\texttt{*show-messages*} and \texttt{*sdk-not-found*}.

\section{Graphics driver entry points}

\texttt{chorus/interop/driver-api} adds
\texttt{cu-graphics-resource}, the \texttt{cu-graphics-register-flags-*} and
\texttt{cu-graphics-map-resource-flags-*} enumerations, and these functions:
\texttt{cu-gl-ctx-create}, \texttt{cu-graphics-gl-register-buffer},
\texttt{cu-graphics-map-resources},
\texttt{cu-graphics-resource-get-mapped-pointer},
\texttt{cu-graphics-resource-set-map-flags},
\texttt{cu-graphics-unmap-resources}, and
\texttt{cu-graphics-unregister-resource}.
It also reexports \texttt{chorus/driver-api}.

\section{What the interop API replaces}

\texttt{chorus/interop/api} reexports \texttt{chorus/api} except the context,
memory-block, and \texttt{defkernel} symbols that the interop packages
replace. The replacements are \texttt{create-cuda-context},
\texttt{with-cuda}, \texttt{defkernel}, and the memory-block operations,
including \texttt{memory-block-vertex-buffer-object} and
\texttt{memory-block-graphic-resource-ptr}.

The example \texttt{interop/examples/nbody.lisp} is the system
\texttt{chorus-interop-examples}. Its package is
\texttt{chorus/interop/examples/nbody}.
